        'zakat.seo.h1': 'How is zakat on money calculated?',
        'zakat.seo.h1_body': 'Zakat is typically calculated as 2.5% of net zakatable wealth once it meets the nisab and a full lunar year (Hawl) has passed. Formula: Zakat = Net wealth × 2.5%.',
        'zakat.seo.h2': 'What is the nisab for zakat?',
        'zakat.seo.h2_body': 'The nisab is the minimum amount of wealth that triggers the obligation of zakat once the Hawl has passed. It is commonly estimated as the equivalent of 85 grams of gold or 595 grams of silver.',
        'zakat.seo.h3': 'What wealth is included in zakat?',
        'zakat.seo.h3_body': '<li>Cash, bank accounts, and savings</li><li>Gold and silver</li><li>Trade goods and merchandise</li><li>Stocks and investments</li><li>Property held for sale</li>',
        'zakat.seo.h4': 'What wealth is generally excluded?',
        'zakat.seo.h4_body': '<li>Personal residence</li><li>Personal vehicle</li><li>Furniture and personal belongings</li><li>Property not intended for sale</li><li>Tools used for work, not for sale</li>',
        'zakat.faq.title': 'Zakat FAQ',
        'zakat.faq.q1': 'How do I calculate zakat on money?',
        'zakat.faq.a1': 'If the wealth meets the nisab and a full lunar year (Hawl) has passed, zakat is calculated at 2.5% of the net zakatable wealth.',
        'zakat.faq.q2': 'What is the rate of zakat on money?',
        'zakat.faq.a2': 'The rate of zakat on money is generally 2.5%.',
        'zakat.faq.q3': 'Is zakat due on salary?',
        'zakat.faq.a3': 'Salary itself is not subject to zakat upon receipt, but whatever is saved from it that meets the nisab and on which a full lunar year passes is included in the zakat calculation.',
        'zakat.faq.q4': 'Is gold subject to zakat?',
        'zakat.faq.a4': 'Gold is subject to zakat once it meets the nisab. Personal jewelry gold has fiqh differences, so refer to the fatwa you follow.',
        'zakat.faq.q5': 'Is zakat due on stocks?',
        'zakat.faq.a5': 'Yes, zakat may be due on stocks depending on the intention (long-term investment, speculation, or trade). They can be included under the investments section in the calculator.',
        'zakat.faq.q6': 'Should I deduct debts from zakat?',
        'zakat.faq.a6': 'Some due debts may be deducted, but the details vary by debt type and timing — this calculator provides a general estimate.',
        'zakat.faq.q7': 'Does this calculator replace consulting a scholar?',
        'zakat.faq.a7': 'No, the calculator helps you estimate, but it does not replace consulting a knowledgeable scholar in special or complex cases.',
        'zakat.howto.step1': 'Determine the nisab — 85g gold or 595g silver at market price.',
        'zakat.howto.step2': 'Sum all your zakatable wealth (cash + gold + investments + receivables).',
        'zakat.howto.step3': 'Subtract debts owed by you to obtain the net zakatable wealth.',
        'zakat.howto.step4': 'Multiply net wealth × 2.5% if it meets the nisab and the Hawl has passed.',
        'zakat.disclaimer.title': 'Important notice',
        'zakat.disclaimer.body': 'This calculator provides a general estimate of zakat based on your inputs. Some details may vary depending on the type of wealth, debts, gold, stocks, or the fatwa followed in your country. For special cases, consult a trusted scholar.',
