        'tasbih.allahu_akbar': 'Allahu Akbar',
        // MSBAHA-SEO-CONTENT-UX-EXPANSION-1 — educational + FAQ block (v=190 bump)
        'tasbih.edu.title': 'What is the Electronic Tasbih?',
        'tasbih.edu.intro': 'The electronic tasbih is a simple digital tool that helps you count Subhanallah, Alhamdulillah, and Allahu Akbar without needing a physical bead tasbih. It runs in your browser, keeps your count during the session, and supports two modes: auto mode for after-prayer dhikr (33 + 33 + 33) and free-counter mode for any other dhikr.',
        'tasbih.howto.title': 'How to Use the Electronic Tasbih',
        'tasbih.howto.intro': 'Follow these simple steps:',
        'tasbih.howto.step1_title': 'Choose your mode',
        'tasbih.howto.step1_desc': 'Pick "Auto Tasbih" for the after-prayer sequence: Subhanallah, Alhamdulillah, Allahu Akbar — each 33 times. Or pick "Free Counter" for any other dhikr like istighfar or salawat on the Prophet ﷺ.',
        'tasbih.howto.step2_title': 'Tap the big circle',
        'tasbih.howto.step2_desc': 'Every tap increases the count by one. In auto mode the counter automatically advances to the next dhikr when you reach 33, so you do not need to do anything extra.',
        'tasbih.howto.step3_title': 'Follow the progress bar',
        'tasbih.howto.step3_desc': 'A bar under the circle shows your position out of 33, and the session total is displayed below, so you can be sure you completed the required count.',
        'tasbih.howto.step4_title': 'Reset whenever you need',
        'tasbih.howto.step4_desc': 'Use "Reset counter" to bring the current dhikr back to 0 without losing the session total, or "Reset session" to start a brand new session from zero.',
        'tasbih.after.title': 'After-Prayer Tasbih',
        'tasbih.after.intro': 'The Prophet ﷺ said: "Whoever glorifies Allah after every prayer thirty-three times, praises Allah thirty-three times, and magnifies Allah thirty-three times — that is ninety-nine — and completes the hundred with: La ilaha illa Allah, Wahdahu la sharika lah, lahu al-mulk wa lahu al-hamd wa Huwa ala kulli shay\'in qadir — his sins will be forgiven even if they were like the foam of the sea." — Reported by Muslim.',
        'tasbih.after.card1_desc': 'Glorifying Allah above any imperfection. Said thirty-three times after the obligatory prayer.',
        'tasbih.after.card2_desc': 'Praising Allah for all His apparent and hidden blessings. Said thirty-three times after the tasbih.',
        'tasbih.after.card3_desc': 'Magnifying Allah, glorified is He. Said thirty-three times, then the count is sealed with the testimony of monotheism to complete the hundred.',
        'tasbih.when.title': 'When to Use the Electronic Tasbih',
        'tasbih.when.intro': 'You can benefit from it in several situations:',
        'tasbih.when.c1_title': 'After the five daily prayers',
        'tasbih.when.c1_desc': 'The most common use: count Subhanallah 33, Alhamdulillah 33, and Allahu Akbar 33, then the testimony of monotheism.',
        'tasbih.when.c2_title': 'Morning and evening adhkar',
        'tasbih.when.c2_desc': 'Count tahlil, istighfar, and salawat on the Prophet ﷺ as part of your morning and evening dhikr routines.',
        'tasbih.when.c3_title': 'Daily istighfar',
        'tasbih.when.c3_desc': 'Set a daily goal — for example 100 istighfars — and count them easily in free-counter mode.',
        'tasbih.when.c4_title': 'Idle and waiting moments',
        'tasbih.when.c4_desc': 'Invest waiting minutes in dhikr — while waiting for an appointment, on public transport, etc.',
        'tasbih.when.c5_title': 'Travel and on the move',
        'tasbih.when.c5_desc': 'A practical alternative to a physical bead tasbih while traveling — works directly on your phone.',
        'tasbih.related.title': 'Related Tools and Worship',
        'tasbih.related.intro': 'Helpful links that complement your daily worship:',
        'tasbih.related.prayer_title': 'Prayer Times',
        'tasbih.related.prayer_desc': 'Know the five daily prayer times in your city so you never miss a tasbih after each prayer.',
        'tasbih.related.azkar_title': 'Adhkar',
        'tasbih.related.azkar_desc': 'The comprehensive adhkar page: morning, evening, sleep, and more.',
        'tasbih.related.qibla_title': 'Qibla Direction',
        'tasbih.related.qibla_desc': 'Find the qibla direction from your location accurately before prayer.',
        'tasbih.related.hijri_title': 'Hijri Date',
        'tasbih.related.hijri_desc': 'Follow today\'s Hijri date and remember the virtuous days such as the White Days.',
        'tasbih.disclaimer.title': 'Note',
        'tasbih.disclaimer.body': 'The electronic tasbih is only a helping tool — the reward is tied to the dhakir\'s intention and presence of heart, not to whether the count is done on a physical tasbih, an electronic one, or on the fingers.',
        'tasbih.faq.title': 'Frequently Asked Questions',
        'tasbih.faq.q1': 'Is the electronic tasbih a bid\'ah (innovation)?',
        'tasbih.faq.a1': 'No. It is merely a tool for counting dhikr, exactly like a physical bead tasbih or counting on the fingers. The principle is that dhikr is Sunnah, and any tool that helps you do it is permissible as long as it does not distract from the goal.',
        'tasbih.faq.q2': 'Does the tasbih save the count after closing the page?',
        'tasbih.faq.a2': 'Currently the count is preserved only during the session. When you reload the page the count starts again — this is intentional so it matches the after-prayer tasbih as a standalone event.',
        'tasbih.faq.q3': 'Why the number 33 after prayer?',
        'tasbih.faq.a3': 'The number 33 comes from the Prophetic hadith: tasbih 33 + tahmid 33 + takbir 33 = 99, then sealed with the testimony of monotheism to complete the hundred. The electronic tasbih in auto mode follows this exact order.',
        'tasbih.faq.q4': 'Can I use it instead of a physical bead tasbih?',
        'tasbih.faq.a4': 'Yes. There is no shar\'i difference between counting on a physical tasbih, an electronic one, or on the fingers — the latter is mentioned in the hadith: "Count with the fingertips, for they will be questioned and made to speak." Choose whatever helps you focus more.',
        'tasbih.faq.q5': 'Does the tasbih work offline?',
        'tasbih.faq.a5': 'Yes, after you open the page once. The site supports offline operation (PWA), so once the page is loaded the tasbih runs locally on your device.',
        'tasbih.faq.q6': 'Is the tasbih free and safe?',
        'tasbih.faq.a6': 'Yes, it is completely free with no registration and no ads inside the tool, and the count stays on your device — nothing is sent to any server.',
        'azkar.count_label': '{count} azkar',
